Z||000002||Formula88||10-21-2001||01:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>NO firebirds are 115x5 we are 100x5<BR>will not fit canbe made to work but right wheels are cheaper and better.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, they're not 5x115, they're 5x4.75.  They're not metric.  I don't remember if it's 4 3/4" exactly, but I do remember them being SAE, not metric.  Also, being a RWD rim instead of FWD, the offset is way different.  <P>I've seen people use them, but you have to swap hubs, etc. to make it work.  Not sure how much is involved.  The procedures may be in the archives.||||reg||1
